<Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />

<.page_shell>
  <section class="relative pt-16 pb-14 pl-10 sm:pl-12 lg:pt-20 lg:pl-48">
    <p class="text-ink/55 text-label mb-6 font-semibold uppercase lg:absolute lg:top-20 lg:left-0 lg:mb-0 lg:w-32 lg:text-right">
      Terms
    </p>

    <h1 class="font-display text-hero max-w-3xl font-normal">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="text-fine text-ink/55 mt-4">Last updated 17 July 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-10 max-w-2xl space-y-8">
      <p class="text-body text-ink/75 font-light">
        These terms govern your use of Nila, operated by Kaguya Media Private
        Limited ("Nila", "we", "us"). By creating an account or using the
        service you agree to them. If you are agreeing on behalf of a firm, you
        confirm you are authorised to bind it.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">What Nila does</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          Nila does a junior accountant's preparation work: you send an
          unstructured mess of documents, and Nila extracts, classifies, and
          drafts structured GST workings — registers, reconciliations, and
          import sheets — and flags the lines that need judgment. Nila is a tool
          that produces drafts for you to review. It is not your accountant,
          auditor, or tax adviser, and using it does not create a
          professional-client relationship with us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">You review; you file</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          Nila drafts, a human approves. Nila does not file returns or submit
          anything to any authority on your behalf. You are responsible for
          reviewing every output before you rely on it, for the accuracy and
          legality of what you ultimately file, and for the professional
          judgment applied to the lines Nila flags. The signature stays yours.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Your responsibilities</h2>
        <ul class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 space-y-2 font-light">
          <li>
            You have the right to upload the documents you send us and to have us
            process them, including any client authorisation required.
          </li>
          <li>
            You keep your login credentials secure and are responsible for
            activity under your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            You will not use Nila unlawfully, to process data you have no right
            to, or in a way that disrupts the service.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          We and our licensors retain all rights in Nila, including its software,
          design, documentation, and branding. You retain ownership of the data
          and documents you provide. You grant us only the limited rights needed
          to host, process, transmit, and display that material to operate the
          service for you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">No warranty</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          The service is provided "as is" and "as available". Automated
          extraction and classification can be wrong, and Nila's flags are aids,
          not guarantees. To the fullest extent permitted by law we disclaim all
          warranties, express or implied, including fitness for a particular
          purpose and that the output is accurate, complete, or compliant. The
          output is a draft for your review — not tax, legal, or accounting
          advice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, Nila is not liable for any
          indirect, incidental, or consequential loss, or for any penalties,
          interest, or tax liability arising from returns you prepare or file
          using our output. Our total liability for any claim relating to the
          service is limited to the fees you paid us for it in the three months
          before the claim arose. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be
          limited under law.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Fees</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          Where the service is paid, fees, billing cycle, and taxes are as set
          out in your order or plan. Fees are exclusive of applicable GST unless
          stated otherwise.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Suspension &amp; termination</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          You may stop using Nila and close your account at any time. We may
          suspend or terminate access if these terms are breached or the service
          is misused. On termination, your data is handled as described in the <.link
            navigate={~p"/privacy"}
            class="text-redink hover:underline"
          >privacy policy</.link>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Governing law</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at
          Chennai, Tamil Nadu have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-body text-ink/75 mt-3 font-light">
          We may update these terms as the service evolves. Material changes will
          be posted here with a new date; continued use after a change means you
          accept the updated terms. Questions go to <a
            href="mailto:hello@nila.tax"
            class="text-redink hover:underline"
          >hello@nila.tax</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</.page_shell>
